# Don't disturb working blocks

If a layout or UI fix for one element would require changing another block that already works, do not change that other block. Leave it as it is.

- Fix only the element that is actually broken or requested.
- Do not restyle, wrap, or rewire a working form, globe, popular destinations panel, search, or backend path as a side effect.
- Shared components (calendar, city input) may be reused as they are; do not change them just because a neighbouring screen needs a different look — adjust only the local layout of the requested block.
- Prefer a local wrapper or props on the requested screen over editing a shared, already-correct block.
